# LA Forward Voter Guide

Civic voter guide for a nonprofit (LA Forward), built pro-bono. Optimize
every decision for **longevity and low maintenance burden**, not
short-term convenience — this must keep working after the original
builders step back, maintained by non-technical staff.

**Stack:** Next.js (App Router) + a **standalone** Sanity Studio. The
Studio lives in its own sibling repo/folder, `studio-la-forward-voter-guide`,
next to this app folder — not embedded, not a route in this app. This app
only fetches published content; it has no `sanity.config.ts`, no
`schemaTypes/`, and no dependency on the `sanity` package.

**Content model:** Region → Race/Measure → Entry. Entry references Race
(one-directional only — never add a reverse `race.entries` array; see
`schemaTypes/race.ts` in the Studio repo for why).

**Locked — don't relitigate without asking the user first:**
- CMS is Sanity, not Contentful/Strapi/other
- Studio is standalone, in `studio-la-forward-voter-guide` — do not embed
  it in or move it into this app
- One nested GROQ query for the whole guide, not per-section queries
- Single `production` dataset, no separate testing dataset
- Time-based ISR (5 min), not a revalidation webhook
- Entry rating: No Recommendation / Recommended / Endorsed (fixed 3 values)
- Measure position: Support / Oppose / No Position

Full reasoning for all of the above: `docs/backend-strategy.md` (note:
the embedded-Studio recommendation in that doc was superseded — see the
amendment at the bottom of that file).
